over a decade of Marvel movie magic 21  films in the MCU dozens of Easter eggs  and hundreds of minutes of action and  emotion it has all led up to this moment  the release of Avengers endgame ahead of  in game's theatrical debut reviews for  the superhero ensemble started hitting  the Internet  critics near and far race to let their  thoughts about in-game be heard and  you'll want to lend them your ear here's  what the critics on Rotten Tomatoes are  saying about Avengers endgame don't  worry you're entering a spoiler free  zone there's a lot riding on Avengers in  game to be a worthy successor to  Avengers infinity war and a capstone to  three phases of the MCU so far  thankfully endgame seems to have EE  succeeded critics say it pays off  everything within itself and much that  preceded it risks of past movies bets  the heroes make here the lengthy runtime  the stakes and storylines the plot we  won't spoil everything  Mashable's angie Han wrote the bet pays  off  the story feels more organic this time  the emotions more earned and the  interpersonal dynamics richer and more  lived-in din of geek called the film a  totally triumphant pay off while susana  pollo a polygon said there's nothing in  game sets up that it doesn't pay off  said David Simms of the Atlantic the  film earns its length not by  overstuffing the frame with opulent  action but by slowing things down and  basking in the charisma of its ensemble  Thanos is demand for a dramatic ending  and infinity war pays off here in all  the right ways russ fisher at birth  movies death agreed rather than closing  things down in game opens everything up  this is a genre film with layers of  overlapping big ideas character  conflicts that could be flat-out  ridiculous if handled with less skill  and deep in jokes featuring dozens of  costume characters ultimately in-game is  an entire movie of payoffs it plays off  and completes thoughts begun in age of  Ultron and Civil War and even in comics  if you thought Avengers infinity war was  heartbreaking you apparently have a big  storm coming with Avengers in game  critics are advising fans to pack some  hankies and wear waterproof mascara when  they head out to see the film as it's  packed with tear-jerking emotions of all  sorts hey it even reportedly made  Captain America himself Chris Evans cry  six times  insiders Kirsten Hakuna wants  moviegoers to hit the theatres prepared  bust out the tissues Marvel fans  Avengers in game is going to make you  laugh cheer aloud tear up multiple times  and cry by the film's in there were  audible sniffles throughout insiders  10:00 a.m. press screening Tuesday  morning in game is an emotional punch  straight to the gut you're going to be  too emotionally distraught by the film's  ending to really nitpick at anything in  endgame viewers won't weep exclusively  out of sadness though as rosy Fletcher  and Richard Jordan at den of geek wrote  in their joint review at times in game  as heartbreaking expect to cry but there  are certain scenes that border on the  euphoric certain character moments  surprises and reveals that hit so hard  in the heart and the head that it feels  like you're MCU drunk even Richard  Roeper of the Chicago sun-times couldn't  help but be moved by in game it's a  serious contender for the crown and it's  the undisputed champion when it comes to  emotional punch Avengers endgame is as  emotionally affecting as any Marvel  movie has ever been okay so we know the  movie will probably make you cry but  that doesn't mean the movie is a sob  fest from start to finish  critics have indicated that in-game  features plenty of the emcee use  trademark humor which helps steady the  sentimentality jake Kleinman of inverse  explained thor delivers some of the best  jokes an end game sometimes without  saying a word the Washington Post's  Michael O'Sullivan concurred saying as  high as the stakes are in endgame it is  also a very funny movie it seems one of  the movie's most prominent strong points  is its ability to mix emotion with  comedy and avoid tipping too far to one  side as the guardians Peter Bradshaw  wrote the sheer enjoyment and fun that  it delivers the pure exotic spectacle  are irresistible as is its insouciant  way of combining the serious and the  comic without the comedy the drama would  not be palatable yet without the earnest  almost childlike belief in the  seriousness of what is at stake the  funny stuff would not work either  National Review critic Kyle Smith might  have said it best when he wrote a sombre  aura gives Avengers in-game its gravitas  but the movie is also funny rousing and  above all endearing where there are  lovers there are haters or in this case  people who didn't fall completely head  over heels for the feature bold and  beautiful as it evidently is the film  still isn't immune from critique though  the vast majority of reviewers Bay  basically gave endgame full marks a few  critics took a more well critical  approach to the film Forbes senior  contributor Scott Mendelssohn wrote that  endgame is flawed and feels as if it  copied certain beats of infinity war  though it's still entertaining and ties  up the threads of the MCU nicely it  doesn't make a ton of internal sense  suffers from narrative claustrophobia  and the action leaves a little to be  desired Avengers in game is a merely OK  MCU movie but there is grace in its  failings Donald Clark of the Irish Times  argued that in-game spends too long  wallowing in its own pomposity and is  short on fun Christian long at glide  magazine called it a subversive  compelling and thoroughly unsatisfying  film that chooses to rely on vacuous  fanservice instead of taking the time to  put any real heart into its storytelling  once certified Rotten review came from  Globe and Mail's Barrie Hertz who wrote  the entire endeavor loses any sense of  emotional stakes or general meaning  beyond the deliverance of crass  fanservice and incomprehensible visuals  it seems that for every fault one could  find in Avengers in game 10 times the  amount of merits exist sure a handful of  critics weren't roused by the superhero  ensemble and that's a-ok but far more  were moved enough to exalt it as a true  achievement and stamp it with perfect or  near-perfect scores  why according to Germaine Lussier with  io9 the film is everything you've ever  dreamed the Marvel movie could be and  then some in versus Jake Kleinman wrote  that the film definitely delivers on its  promise of big action and bigger heart  with its third act feeling quote unlike  anything we've ever seen before in the  history of the MCU as the movie finally  ended I felt different almost as if I  was glowing like brie Larson's Captain  Marvel the result of eleven years of  world building has arrived and it feels  like nothing will be the same again in  his review of endgame Nick Johnston at  vanya land said the film is everything a  fan could want and feels like an actual  ending to the story writing it doesn't  feel like a teaser for another movie  later on down the line its content with  satisfying you the devoted in the here  and now the Salt Lake Tribune Sean P  means offered a similar analysis writing  Avengers in game delivers everything  Marvel fans will enjoy and not much that  they expect Earth's Mightiest Heroes  fulfill their promise in  installment that takes a decade of  superhero storytelling and ties it  together into an astounding emotional  conclusion check out one of our newest  videos right here  plus even more looper videos about  Avengers in game art coming soon  subscribe to our YouTube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  [Music]
 

